\description{
Import the Thünen-Institut exports of the German groundfish survey off
Greenland (R/V Walther Herwig, ICES survey code \code{GER(GRL)-GFS-Q4}) into
pax-shaped tables, and the steps of the old East Greenland index
(\code{05-redfish/R/Get_Data/Greenland_Cochran.R}) as explicit functions.
}
\details{
The Thünen export tables are:
\describe{
\item{StatFi}{station metadata (\code{STATID}, \code{JAHR}, \code{STATION},
\code{AREA} 21 West / 27 East Greenland, \code{STRATUMNR})}
\item{NetzFi}{hauls (\code{NETZID}, positions \code{GBFANGB}/\code{GLFANGB}
(start) and \code{GBHIEV}/\code{GLHIEV} (end) as \code{DDMMmm} + hemisphere,
\code{DISTANZ} in nautical miles, depths)}
\item{FishFi}{total catch per station and species (\code{FISHID},
\code{GESAMTKG}, \code{GESAMTSTCK}), e.g. \code{CatchesNorvegicus.csv}}
\item{LengFi}{length frequencies (\code{LENGID}, \code{LAENGE}, the cm-below
class + 0.5, \code{LANZAHL} the number measured, \code{SEX}), e.g.
\code{LengthFreqNorvegicus.csv}}
}
Files are recognised by their id column (\code{STATID}, \code{NETZID},
\code{FISHID}, \code{LENGID}), so both the comma-separated CSV layout and the
newer xlsx layout (\code{StatFi.xlsx}, \code{NetzFi_*.xlsx}, \code{FishFi*.xlsx},
\code{LengFi_*.xlsx}) can be read. Files of the same table are row-bound.
Column names are matched ignoring case; the CSV NetzFi columns
\code{depthmin1}/\code{depthmax1}/\code{depthmin2}/\code{depthmax2}/\code{timebeginning}/
\code{timeend} are read as the xlsx \code{TIEFEMIN}/\code{TIEFEMAX}/\code{FTMIN}/
\code{FTMAX}/\code{SZANF}/\code{SZENDE}. \code{-9} is missing.

The tables are kept apart from the MFRI \code{station} and \code{ldist} tables
(\code{ger_station}, \code{ger_ldist}, \code{ger_catch}), as the stations follow
other conventions (a German stratum, positions that need fixing, a fixed
swept area in the index) and the pax_si_* functions take the station and
ldist tables as arguments. They can be combined with the MFRI tables with
\code{dplyr::union_all()} after selecting common columns.
}
